Implementation Notes
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   This file is used by the SPICE system as follows: programs that make
   use of this kernel must ``load'' the kernel, normally during program
   initialization. The SPICE routine FURNSH loads a kernel file into
   the pool as shown below.

      CALL FURNSH ( 'frame_kernel_name; )    -- FORTRAN
      furnsh_c ( "frame_kernel_name" );      -- C
      cspice_furnsh, frame_kernel_name       -- IDL
      cspice_furnsh( 'frame_kernel_name' )   -- MATLAB

   Once the file has been loaded, the SPICE routine GETFOV (getfov_c in
   C, cspice_getfov in IDL and MATLAB) can be used to retrieve FOV
   parameters for a given instrument or structure.

   This file was created and may be updated with a text editor or word
   processor.


Naming Conventions
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   All names referencing values in this IK file start with the
   characters `INS' followed by the NAIF Hayabusa2 ID number (-37)
   followed by a NAIF three digit ID code for one of ONC camera head (ONC-T,
   ONC-W1, ONC-W2):

      HAYABUSA2_ONC-T       -37100
      HAYABUSA2_ONC-W1      -37110
      HAYABUSA2_ONC-W2      -37120

   The remainder of the keyword name is an underscore character
   followed by the unique name of the data item. For example, the
   boresight direction of HAYABUSA2_ONC-T is specified by:

      INS-37100_BORESIGHT

   The upper bound on the length of the name of any data item is 32
   characters.

   If the same item is included in more than one file, or if the same
   item appears more than once within a single file, the latest value
   supersedes any earlier values.


Instrument Description
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   The optical navigation camera (ONC) system on board the Hayabusa2
   consists of three individual framing CCD cameras, ONC-T for a telescopic
   nadir view, ONC-W1 for a wide-angle nadir view, and ONC-W2 for a
   wide- angle slant view will be used to observe the surface of Ryugu.
   The cameras will be used to measure the global asteroid shape, local
   morphologies, and visible spectroscopic properties [3-2].
   For more detailed description, please refer [3-1], [3-2] and [3-3].


Optical Parameters
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   The following ONC optical parameters are included
   in the data section below, taken from [3-2] and [3-3]:

      -------------------------------------------------------
             parameter        ONC-T       ONC-W1      ONC-W2
      -------------------------------------------------------
      Focal Length (1), mm    120.50      10.22       10.34
      f/ratio                 f/9.05 (2)  f/9.6       f/9.6
      IFOV, mrad (3)          0.1074      1.1882      1.1742
      -------------------------------------------------------

   (1) Precise FOV estimation by using distortion-corrected image requires
       these "Focal lengths". The coefficients and procedures for the
       distortion-correction are described in [3-1].

   (2) The effect of FF lamps is considered (f/ratio without FF lamps is
        f/8.0).

   (3) IFOV is computed as the mean pixel resolution from the FOV and the
       number of pixels in X and Y direction:

       e. g.)
          IFOV (ONC-W1) = FOV / number of pixels = 69.71 deg / 1024 pixel
                        = 0.06808 deg / pixel = 1.1882 mrad / pixel
          where the value of FOV is described in [3-1] and section of "FOV
          Definitions".

   Angular size values in the keywords are given in radians.

   \begindata

      INS-37100_FOCAL_LENGTH         = ( 120.50      )
      INS-37100_F/RATIO              = (   9.05      )
      INS-37100_IFOV                 = (   0.0001074 )

      INS-37110_FOCAL_LENGTH         = (  10.22      )
      INS-37110_F/RATIO              = (   9.6       )
      INS-37110_IFOV                 = (   0.0011882 )

      INS-37120_FOCAL_LENGTH         = (  10.34      )
      INS-37120_F/RATIO              = (   9.6       )
      INS-37120_IFOV                 = (   0.0011742 )

  \begintext


Detector CCD Parameters
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   The ONC detector parameters are included in the data section below,
   taken from [3-1] and [3-2]:

      -------------------------------------------------------
             parameter          ONC-T      ONC-W1      ONC-W2
      -------------------------------------------------------
      Pixel Size, microns
          Cross-track [mm]      0.013      0.013       0.013
          Along-track [mm]      0.013      0.013       0.013
      Detector Array Size
          Cross-track            1024       1024        1024
          Along-track            1024       1024        1024
      Detector Array Center
          Cross-track           512.5      512.5       512.5
          Along-track           512.5      512.5       512.5
      -------------------------------------------------------

   The values are given in mm for PIXEL_SIZE keywords and in counts
   for PIXEL_SAMPLES, PIXEL_LINES, and CCD_CENTER keywords.

   The values of PIXEL_SAMPLES and PIXEL_LINES are equal to the diameter of
   each camera head, in counts.

   \begindata

      INS-37100_PIXEL_SIZE           = ( 0.013, 0.013 )
      INS-37100_PIXEL_SAMPLES        = ( 1024 )
      INS-37100_PIXEL_LINES          = ( 1024 )
      INS-37100_CCD_CENTER           = ( 512.5, 512.5 )

      INS-37110_PIXEL_SIZE           = ( 0.013, 0.013 )
      INS-37110_PIXEL_SAMPLES        = ( 1024 )
      INS-37110_PIXEL_LINES          = ( 1024 )
      INS-37110_CCD_CENTER           = ( 512.5, 512.5 )

      INS-37120_PIXEL_SIZE           = ( 0.013, 0.013 )
      INS-37120_PIXEL_SAMPLES        = ( 1024 )
      INS-37120_PIXEL_LINES          = ( 1024 )
      INS-37120_CCD_CENTER           = ( 512.5, 512.5 )

   \begintext


Wavelength Ranges and Filter Parameters
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   This section contains assignments specifying wavelength range and other
   filter parameters of ONC optics and filters.

      -------------------------------------------------------------------------
        Camera   Band Center,   Bandwidth,       Quantum          Transmittance
        Head     nanometers     nanometers (1)   Efficiency (2)   (2), (3)
      -------------------------------------------------------------------------
        ONC-T    545            482              0.968            0.254
        ONC-W1   630            142              0.942            0.0605
        ONC-W2   595            155              0.951            0.238
      -------------------------------------------------------------------------

      -------------------------------------------------------------------------
        ONC-T        Band Center,   Bandwidth,       Band Name    Transmittance
        Filter No.   nanometers     nanometers (1)                (4)
      -------------------------------------------------------------------------
        1            390.413         45              ul           0.676
        2            775            850              Wide         0.879
        3            549.020         28              v            0.797
        4            700.384         28              w            0.874
        5            858.947         42              x            0.900
        6            590.160         10              Na           0.872
        7            949.697         57              p            0.893
        8            479.773         25              b            0.954
      -------------------------------------------------------------------------

      (1) The bandwidth in above tables is defined in terms of Full Width at
          Half Maximum (FWHM) values, as described in [3-1].

      (2) The quantum efficiency and the transmittance values are shown as the
          mean of FWHM for reference.

      (3) The transmittance values of the first table account for both the
          optics and ND filter at the "Band Center".

   The set of assignments below specifies wavelength center and bandwidth for
   each filter, with units the same as in the table above.

   \begindata

      INS-37100_FILTER_BANDCENTER    = (  545      )
      INS-37100_FILTER_BANDWIDTH     = (  482      )
      INS-37100_FILTER_QE            = (    0.968  )
      INS-37100_FILTER_TRANSMITTANCE = (    0.254  )

      INS-37110_FILTER_BANDCENTER    = (  630      )
      INS-37110_FILTER_BANDWIDTH     = (  142      )
      INS-37110_FILTER_QE            = (    0.942  )
      INS-37110_FILTER_TRANSMITTANCE = (    0.0605 )

      INS-37120_FILTER_BANDCENTER    = (  595      )
      INS-37120_FILTER_BANDWIDTH     = (  155      )
      INS-37120_FILTER_QE            = (    0.951  )
      INS-37120_FILTER_TRANSMITTANCE = (    0.238  )

   \begintext


FOV Definitions
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   This section contains definitions for each of ONC camera heads.
   These definitions are provided in a format consistent required by the
   SPICE (CSPICE) function GETFOV (getfov_c).

   Each of ONC camera heads has a square FOV:

      --------------------------------------------
         Camera     FOV
         Head       (degrees)
      --------------------------------------------
         ONC-T       6.302 x  6.302
         ONC-W1     69.71  x 69.71
         ONC-W2     68.89  x 68.89
      --------------------------------------------

   For each of the frames, the boresight vector, along the +Z axis of
   instrument frame, was scaled to be equal to the focal length.
   The reference vector is a unit vector along the +Y axis of the frame.

   \begindata

      INS-37100_FOV_FRAME            = 'HAYABUSA2_ONC-T'
      INS-37100_FOV_SHAPE            = 'RECTANGLE'
      INS-37100_BORESIGHT            = ( 0.0     0.0   120.50 )
      INS-37100_FOV_CLASS_SPEC       = 'ANGLES'
      INS-37100_FOV_REF_VECTOR       = ( 0.0     1.0     0.0  )
      INS-37100_FOV_REF_ANGLE        = ( 3.151 )
      INS-37100_FOV_CROSS_ANGLE      = ( 3.151 )
      INS-37100_FOV_ANGLE_UNITS      = 'DEGREES'

      INS-37110_FOV_FRAME            = 'HAYABUSA2_ONC-W1'
      INS-37110_FOV_SHAPE            = 'RECTANGLE'
      INS-37110_BORESIGHT            = ( 0.0     0.0    10.22 )
      INS-37110_FOV_CLASS_SPEC       = 'ANGLES'
      INS-37110_FOV_REF_VECTOR       = ( 0.0     1.0     0.0  )
      INS-37110_FOV_REF_ANGLE        = ( 34.855 )
      INS-37110_FOV_CROSS_ANGLE      = ( 34.855 )
      INS-37110_FOV_ANGLE_UNITS      = 'DEGREES'

      INS-37120_FOV_FRAME            = 'HAYABUSA2_ONC-W2'
      INS-37120_FOV_SHAPE            = 'RECTANGLE'
      INS-37120_BORESIGHT            = ( 0.0     0.0    10.38 )
      INS-37120_FOV_CLASS_SPEC       = 'ANGLES'
      INS-37120_FOV_REF_VECTOR       = ( 0.0     1.0     0.0  )
      INS-37120_FOV_REF_ANGLE        = ( 34.445 )
      INS-37120_FOV_CROSS_ANGLE      = ( 34.445 )
      INS-37120_FOV_ANGLE_UNITS      = 'DEGREES'

   \begintext


